# Privacy Policy for Pewhipee

Last updated: September 1, 2026

Pewhipee is a memory-game app for iPhone and iPad. It builds puzzles from photographs already on your device.

## What we collect

We do not collect personal information. Pewhipee has no account, no server, and no analytics. We do not sell data. We do not show ads.

## Photos

If you allow Photos access, Pewhipee reads pictures on this device to build games. Copies stay in the app’s own storage on this device. Originals in Photos are never changed. You can delete Pewhipee’s copies in Settings. Today’s challenge may borrow one library photo for the puzzle and let it go unless you keep it.

## Microphone

Talking Memories can record a short story if you allow the microphone. Recordings stay on this device.

## Location

Map Memory uses location already stored in a photo, not live GPS from your iPhone, to grade where you drop a pin. That information stays on this device.

## Notifications

Optional daily reminders are scheduled on this device. We do not send push notifications from a server.

## Sharing

If you send a challenge, the system share sheet sends a picture you chose (for example through Messages or AirDrop). That transfer is between you and the person you send it to. Pewhipee does not operate a server in the middle.

## Children

Pewhipee does not collect data from anyone, including children.

